From: Yeye B.B.C. <19569343+yeyebbc@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8750: Park the UFS symbol clocks at XO

The factory TB522FU UFS driver switches the RX0, RX1 and TX0 symbol
clock muxes to the crystal reference in Hibern8. It selects the PHY
outputs again when exiting Hibern8. The SM8750 GCC describes the same
three muxes with the same PHY and reference selector values. Its
ordinary mux operations leave the selection unchanged at gate time.

Use the existing Qualcomm PHY mux operations to select the PHY when a
symbol clock is enabled and park it at XO when it is disabled. This
follows the pattern Jagadeesh Kona proposed for Glymur. Keep the same
clock IDs, branch gates, and device tree inputs.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-clk/20260915-glymur-ufs-clk-changes-v2-2-d0aa1c60c269@oss.qualcomm.com/
Link: https://github.com/lenovo-basements/android_kernel_lenovo_sm8750/blob/210981a0ad749c30080b853d31bc009d9db0592d/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-ufs.c
Signed-off-by: Yeye B.B.C. <19569343+yeyebbc@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8750.c | 69 +++++++++++--------------------------------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 51 deletions(-)

